{
  "abstract": "A qualified finite sequence-routing formalization connecting the complete source binary rows with padded elementary customer routes and exact transition cost. For fixed valid slots, explicit zero-depot clock/travel conditions give continuous timing feasibility through the earliest-schedule recurrence and an attained minimum total return over timing assignments. Capacity and global route optimization are outside scope.",
